# T32 (F11) example only — NOT installed by any script. F11 stays Proposed.
#
# Copy to /etc/systemd/system/ikbeneenappel-web.service.d/secrets.conf (and the
# same drop-in for ikbeneenappel-refresh.service) when the owner authorizes the
# encrypted-delivery rollout. Until then the units keep using the plaintext
# EnvironmentFile alone, and this file changes nothing.
#
# What it does: the ciphertext lives in /etc/ikbeneenappel/secrets.enc
# (senv1:… envelope from lib/secret-store.ts, root-owned 0600); the unlock key
# arrives as a systemd credential from /etc/ikbeneenappel/.unlock-key
# (base64, root-owned 0600, never in Git, never in the backup). Boot opens the
# envelope into memory with $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY/secrets-unlock and injects
# only the values each subsystem needs. Nonsecret configuration stays in the
# existing EnvironmentFile. Absent credential fails closed.
#
# [Service]
# LoadCredential=secrets-unlock:/etc/ikbeneenappel/.unlock-key
# # SecretsEncPath is read by the (future, authorized) boot path; today it is
# # documentation only and no code reads it.
# Environment=SECRETS_ENC_PATH=/etc/ikbeneenappel/secrets.enc
